{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sampling lives in module "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", and sampling by session uses "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". Nothing is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sampled until the app gives the tracker its samplers:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import Sessions","","struct Scrolled: Event {","    var offset: Int","}","","let tracker = Tracker(","    enrichers: [.sessions()],","    samplers: [.events(of: Scrolled.self, rate: 0.1), .sessions(rate: 0.5)]",")","tracker.track(Scrolled(offset: 120))  \/\/ if kept, its record's context[SampleRateKey.self]?.value is 0.05"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Samplers","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Samplers"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".events(of:rate:)"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps each event of a type with the probability its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SampleRate"},{"type":"text","text":" gives."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":".events(where:rate:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does the same for each record a predicate selects. Both decide each event","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on its own.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":".sessions(rate:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" keeps or drops every record of a session alike, its ","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionStarted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionEnded","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with it.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":".grouped(by:rate:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" does the same for the groups that any context key’s values make."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A rate is in 0 … 1. A literal outside that range, or ","type":"text"},{"code":"SampleRate(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" given one, traps;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"SampleRate(checked:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" throws ","type":"text"},{"code":"InvalidSampleRate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead. A record is kept only if every sampler","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that applies to it keeps it. A kept record carries the product of their rates as its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"SampleRateKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so a destination can count it as ","type":"text"},{"code":"1 \/ value","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" records. A record that no sampler","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"applies to is always kept and carries no key.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"When-sampling-runs","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"When sampling runs"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The tracker’s worker samples each record after its enrichers, whose keys a sampler can read, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"before its consent and its store. So a dropped event is never held, written to disk or delivered.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Each drop is reported on ","type":"text"},{"code":"samplingDropReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", merged into one report per event type while unread,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as rejections are.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The decisions come from the tracker’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"samplingSeed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", drawn from the system’s random number","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"generator once per tracker unless you pass one. They are the same on every platform and Swift","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"release, so with the seed fixed, which events are kept is fixed too:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let tracker = Tracker(samplers: [.events(of: Scrolled.self, rate: 0.1)], samplingSeed: 42)","for offset in 0 ..< 100 {","    tracker.track(Scrolled(offset: offset))","}","await tracker.finish()","for await report in tracker.samplingDropReports {","    print(report)  \/\/ Scrolled: 89 sampled out","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A session’s decision is made from the seed and the session’s identifier alone, so nothing records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it. The sampler keeps only the current session’s decision, in memory, and never writes the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identifier anywhere. Records that a store recovered from an earlier run were sampled in that run,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and come back in the top-level context, without their rate."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"article","sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent\/samplingevents"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents"},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Sampling Events","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Keep a seeded fraction of the events a tracker tracks, event by event or a whole session at once.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow"],"generated":true,"title":"Guides","anchor":"Guides"}],"references":{"doc://Trackers/documentation/Trackers":{"title":"Trackers","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/trackers","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","abstract":[]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ConsentGating":{"title":"Consent Gating","type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/consentgating","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","abstract":[{"text":"Deliver an event only once the user grants the purpose it is collected for.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Vendor-neutral analytics for Swift: typed events, tracked by a tracker and delivered in batches to any number of destinations."}],"title":"Traffluent","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SessionsAndStandardContext":{"title":"Sessions and Standard Context","type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/sessionsandstandardcontext","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","abstract":[{"text":"Stamp every event with its session and with the app, device, system, locale and network it was tracked on.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/AutomaticTracking":{"kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Track screen views, control activations and the app’s lifecycle without a call at each place they happen.","type":"text"}],"title":"Automatic Tracking","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/automatictracking","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/PersistingRecords":{"title":"Persisting Records","type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","abstract":[{"text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so a record the app tracked survives the process ending.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/DefiningEvents":{"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Derive an event’s conformances and schema from its declaration with "},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and constrain which values its properties may hold."}],"title":"Defining Events","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/definingevents","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingPlanWorkflow":{"title":"Exporting and Checking a Tracking Plan","type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingplanworkflow","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow","abstract":[{"text":"Export the JSON Schema of every event an app tracks, commit it, and fail the build when the events stop matching it.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Sessions/documentation/Sessions":{"title":"Sessions","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/sessions","identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","abstract":[]}}}